HST Office: the ribbon chevron shows only when a group is folded, and what it folds is reached from the keyboard.

The chevron of a ribbon tab is a child of the box whose groups it folds. Once hidden it counted as a folded group, so
the box showed it again with every group on the ribbon, and a click opened an empty popup. The groups to fold are now
found from the width of all of them: when they all fit there is no chevron, otherwise the chevron keeps its place and
the groups fold from the end. A KeyTip that opens the chevron or a folded tab menu puts KeyTips on the commands in
the popup; Esc closes it.

